   161	
   162	In this section, we introduce an example that will be used throughout the paper to illustrate
   163	our approach and highlight the limitations of existing approaches. This example describes a bug
   164	that happened when a user attempted to increase the stock of medicine recorded in a personal
   165	medication management app, Calendula [1] . Figure 1a shows the four steps required to reproduce
   166	this bug. However, in the original bug report, only two steps were included ( 푠 1 and 푠 2 ) while the
   167	other two were omitted ( 푠 푥 and 푠 푦 ). Figure 2 displays the necessary UI events for reproducing the
   168	steps in the app where each 푒 푥 denotes a click event performed on the app’s UI . Specifically, to
   169	reproduce the four steps, one needs to follow the event path 푒 1 → 푒 2 → 푒 3 → 푒 4 shown in Figure 2.
